\import{macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}

\taxon{Definition}
\title{RLVR protocol}
\tag{ftip}
\tag{rlvr}
\tag{post-training}

\p{An \strong{RLVR protocol} is a post-training protocol that repeats the
following operations:}

\ol{
  \li{sample a prompt or task instance;}
  \li{generate one or more responses from a behavior policy;}
  \li{run declared verifiers and record their evidence;}
  \li{convert verified results into credit;}
  \li{apply a policy update subject to the protocol's constraints.}
}

\p{This is a \strong{cross-paper operational family}. It is not a source
definition owned by one algorithm. DeepSeekMath introduces GRPO in
\citet{Section 4.1}{shao2024deepseekmath}. DeepSeek-R1 specifies its
R1-Zero procedure in \citet{Section 2.2}{guo2025deepseek}. DAPO changes
sampling, clipping, normalization, and length treatment in
\citet{Sections 2--3}{yu2025dapo}.}

\p{A claim about RLVR must name the member of this family. Otherwise the
rollout law, reward, and update are ambiguous.}
